From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:26:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input-helper: Take a touchpad to be present under Camino

touchpad_is_present looks for a touchpad among the XInput devices, and on
a Wayland display it says there is none. The media-keys plugin then shows
"Touchpad disabled" for the touchpad toggle key and leaves touchpad-enabled
as it was.

Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, applies
org.mate.peripherals-touchpad to the touchpads it finds itself. When
MATE_WM_NAME is Camino, say that a touchpad is present, so that the key
toggles the setting. Without that variable, nothing changes.
---
 plugins/common/msd-input-helper.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plugins/common/msd-input-helper.c b/plugins/common/msd-input-helper.c
index b6ca524..49d7617 100644
--- a/plugins/common/msd-input-helper.c
+++ b/plugins/common/msd-input-helper.c
@@ -115,6 +115,13 @@ touchpad_is_present (void)
         guint i;
         gboolean retval;
 
+        /* Under Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, there is no XInput
+         * to ask. Camino applies org.mate.peripherals-touchpad to the
+         * touchpads it has, so say there is one, and the key that toggles
+         * touchpad-enabled writes it. */
+        if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Camino") == 0)
+                return TRUE;
+
         if (!GDK_IS_X11_DISPLAY (gdk_display_get_default ()))
                 return FALSE;
 
